          "inheritance": "de novo",
          "parental_testing_statement": "DNA was extracted from the peripheral blood leukocytes of the patient, her parents, and her grandparents. Patient homozygous (A/A) for TNFAIP3 c.305A > G (NM_001270507.2); mother (II-2) heterozygous (A/G); father (II-1) homozygous for the reference allele (G/G), suggesting a deletion. CNV analysis of WES data (EXCAVATOR2) showed a single de novo 187 kb microdeletion within TNFAIP3; genome-wide SNP array of the patient and her father validated a de novo 119 kb microdeletion; only the patient harbored the 119 kb deletion. Both WES and CNV analyses indicated that the patient had lost the paternal allele of the TNFAIP3 gene.",
